#: sdlc/processes/test-data-curation.bpmn:122
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "BOUND BY THE CONTENT TYPE, so no `calledElement` is written here: each specialisation process belongs to the layer that owns its content type, and a lower layer cannot name a higher layer\\'s process. The specialisation is the one Task_DetermineSpecialisation found; so no single content-type `calledElement` is hardcoded here: the activity names `test-data-sets`, and each content-type adapter supplies its own specialisation subprocess. `fhir-templating` (`FHIR_TEMPLATING_SPECIALISATION`) is one named specialisation for FHIR IG / DAK content (MeasureReport cohorts, questionnaire responses, bundle templates) — named as such, not the platform design; document folios (`markdown-fixture`), proof folios (`lean-counterexample`), and tabular cohorts (`tabular-cohort`) supply their own."
msgstr ""

#: sdlc/processes/test-data-curation.bpmn:97
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "Calls `Process_SmeTestDataReview` (`sdlc/processes/sme-test-data-review.bpmn`) so a human SME in a `judgementOnly` lane reviews each worked case (`decision-support`) or cohort plus expected value (`indicator-definition`) and records an attributable `sme-case-verdict/1.0.0` node."
msgstr ""

