#. Diagram label
msgid "Not yours — left alone"
msgstr ""

#: sdlc/processes/test-data-curation.bpmn:161
#. Diagram label
msgid "Open the bean"
msgstr ""

#: sdlc/processes/test-data-curation.bpmn:148
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "Parse the file with `discriminateTestDataSet` (`schemas/sdlc/test-data.ts`) to confirm a consumer can tell fixed from generated from the file content alone (never the path), verify `verifyGeneratedSetDigest` on generated sets, and bind the resulting `TestDataRef` (`toTestDataRef`) into the `test-plan/v1` case."
msgstr ""

#: sdlc/processes/test-data-curation.bpmn:178
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "Process_BeanClose: end the bean in a state that says why — complete and archive it, scrap it with its reasons and archive it, or record the blocker and hand it back. The one place resolve and archive are drawn; placed straight before the end so the engine's resolve sees nothing left but the archive step."
msgstr ""

#: sdlc/processes/test-data-curation.bpmn:162
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "Process_BeanOpen: check before you create, find out whose the bean is, and claim it — or leave it alone when it is someone else's. The one place a claim is drawn; the gateway after this reads which end it reached."
msgstr ""

#: sdlc/processes/test-data-curation.bpmn:113
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "Read the folio's `contentType` and the `specialisation` registered for it (`TestDataSpecialisationSchema` in `schemas/sdlc/test-data.ts`): `fhir-templating` for FHIR IG and DAK content, `markdown-fixture` for document folios, `lean-counterexample` for proof folios, `tabular-cohort` for aggregate indicator tables. None registered stops here and says so, rather than guessing one."
msgstr ""

#: sdlc/processes/test-data-curation.bpmn:168
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "Reads which end Process_BeanOpen reached. `claimed`: the bean is in progress and this process works it. `not yours`: a sibling session or a human holds it, nothing was written to it, and this process stops here rather than work a bean it does not own (bean-coordination)."
msgstr ""

#: sdlc/processes/test-data-curation.bpmn:132
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "Record `contentType`, `specialisation`, `template`, `params`, `seed`, and the canonical `sha256` digest (`computeGeneratedSetDigest`) with `$schema: \"test-data-generated/1.0.0\"` and `kind: \"generated\"` in the instance's declared `test-data-generated` directory. Never store materialised records."
msgstr ""

